# Unit Testing

> This file previously described Vitest, React Testing Library, a root `tests/`
> directory and a 70% coverage gate. None of that was ever true in this repo,
> and following it produced seven test files importing an uninstalled `vitest`
> that therefore never ran. It now describes the real setup.

## Runner

`yarn test` → `scripts/test.sh` → Node's built-in test runner with native TS
stripping:

```bash
node --experimental-strip-types --import ./scripts/test-loader.mjs --test $(find src -name '*.test.ts' | sort)
```

Zero test dependencies. Requires Node 22+.

## Conventions

- **Location:** co-located beside the code, `src/**/thing.test.ts` — not a root
  `tests/` directory.
- **Glob:** the runner matches `*.test.ts` only. A `.test.tsx` file is silently
  skipped, which is why there are no component/DOM tests. Extract logic into a
  pure module and test that instead.
- **Imports need the explicit extension**, preceded by the ts-expect-error the
  strip-types loader requires:

  ```ts
  import assert from "node:assert/strict";
  import { describe, it } from "node:test";
  // @ts-expect-error -- Node strip-types needs the extension.
  import { parseChartingFee } from "./parseFee.ts";
  ```

- **Assertions:** `node:assert/strict` — `assert.equal`, `assert.deepEqual`,
  `assert.throws`, `assert.rejects`, `assert.match`. There is no `expect`.
- **Typecheck:** `tsconfig.json` excludes `**/*.test.ts`, so test files are not
  typechecked today. That is why the `@ts-expect-error` above is tolerated.
- **Zod schemas:** at least one valid and one invalid case each.
- No `test.only` merged to main.

## What to test

Pure functions, schemas and reducers — which is most of `src/services/**` and
`src/features/**/lib/**`.

For code that touches Supabase, inject the client and use the in-memory fake at
`src/services/admin_ai/testing/fakeDb.ts` rather than reaching for a mocking
library. It records calls, so a test can assert what was *not* done.

For AI work, add a golden case to the relevant `goldenCases.test.ts`: a raw
model output in, the parsed decision asserted out — including adversarial and
malformed inputs, not just the happy path.

## Commands

```bash
yarn test        # whole suite
yarn typecheck   # tsc --noEmit
node --experimental-strip-types --import ./scripts/test-loader.mjs --test src/path/to/one.test.ts
```

## End-to-end

Browser and database coverage lives in `e2e/` and runs on Playwright against a
local Supabase (`yarn e2e`, see `playwright.config.ts`). It sits outside `src/`
deliberately, so this runner does not pick it up.
